> 
> Can {fa'u} be used with numbers?
> 
> (AKA: jbofihe doesn't like it but I don't know how much to make of
> that)

L*(1) parsers (all of them, I believe) have Problems with joi.
Here's how to make it work with the official parser and/or jbofihe:

mi rirni ci da noi verba li 12 lo'o fa'u li 10 lo'o fa'u li 4

As solving this problem only requires two tokens of lookahead, it's
pretty sad.  This is one of the reasons I'm happy with camxes
(http://teddyb.org/~rlpowell//hobbies/lojban/grammar/), which has no
problem with this at all (and needed no additional work to "fix"
this "problem").

